cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use strider in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "strider: open nucleic-acid thermodynamics, TMSD kinetics, and sequence design"
abstract: >-
  strider is a Python library for the thermodynamics and kinetics of DNA/RNA
  circuits: nearest-neighbor free energies, Zuker/McCaskill secondary-structure
  prediction, multi-strand tube equilibria, toehold-mediated strand-displacement
  kinetics, reaction-network derivation, and gradient-based sequence design — with
  an Na+ x Mg2+ x temperature salt model and no external thermodynamic
  dependencies, under an MIT license.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Venegas
    given-names: Emilio
    email: emiliovenegas10@gmail.com
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/EmilioVenegas/strider"
url: "https://github.com/EmilioVenegas/strider"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-06-16
keywords:
  - nucleic-acid thermodynamics
  - DNA computing
  - toehold-mediated strand displacement
  - RNA secondary structure
  - sequence design
  - nearest-neighbor model
